`ifndef HI3516AV300_CRG_RDL
`define HI3516AV300_CRG_RDL

regfile eCRG {
    name = "Clock and reset generator (CRG), Hi3516A V300";
    desc = "    PERI_CRG clock/reset generator registers at 0x12010000 (CRG). The names follow the HiSilicon scheme PERI_CRGn with offset = n x 4; the PLL registers are called PERI_CRG_PLLn (n = 0..7) and two status registers PERI_CRG_PLL121/122. Data sheet: Hi3516AV300 Professional Smart IP Camera SoC User Guide, document version 01 (2019-09-15), the original Chinese edition (watermarked), chapter 3.1 (reset), 3.2 (clock), register overview 3.2.5 and register descriptions 3.2.6 (printed pages 3-2..3-58). Only the registers listed in the data sheet exist here (55 registers). Read from the PDF text (pdftotext -raw, free of the watermark) and cross-checked with the layout dump `hi3516av300--Hi3516AV300-Datasheet.txt` lines 6432..9952. Checked on 2026-11-10.

    Reset: every module has a soft reset request bit: 1 = reset, 0 = deassert. The module reset is not released automatically, so software must write 0 again. After a global soft reset request the circuit needs at least 360 system clocks to complete; no new request may be issued meanwhile. The reset state of TDE, VGS, VIPROC, VPSS, GDC, GZIP and NNIE can be read back in PERI_CRG_PLL121.

    Clock tree facts for bring-up. XIN is a 24 MHz crystal, RTC_XIN 32.768 kHz. Four PLLs, each with two registers: APLL PERI_CRG_PLL0/1, DPLL PERI_CRG_PLL2/3, EPLL PERI_CRG_PLL4/5, VPLL PERI_CRG_PLL6/7. FOUTVCO = 24 MHz x (fbdiv + frac/2^24) / refdiv (must be 800 MHz..3.2 GHz), FOUTPOSTDIV = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2) with postdiv1 >= postdiv2, further outputs FOUT1PH0/2/3/4 = VCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2 x 2/4/6/8). Reset values give APLL 1800 MHz VCO / 900 MHz POSTDIV, DPLL 2376 / 594, EPLL 1056 / 528, VPLL 1104 / 552 MHz (data sheet Fig. 3-3). Fig. 3-3 marks the EPLL and VPLL (grey) as user-programmable and the APLL and DPLL as fixed. PLL change procedure (3.2.4.1): switch every consumer to a non-PLL (or another PLL) clock, change the PLL registers, wait 0.1 ms, poll PERI_CRG_PLL122 until the PLL reports locked (the data sheet says bits [10:0], only [3:0] exist), then switch back.
    Muxes (all reset to the 24 MHz crystal where there is one): Cortex-A7 PERI_CRG32[2:0] a7_cksel (24/600/792/900 MHz), DDR PERI_CRG32[5:3] ddr_cksel (24/360/396/450 MHz or EPLL POSTDIV), SYSAXI PERI_CRG32[7:6] (24/200/300 MHz), SYSCFG PERI_CRG32[8] (24/148.5 MHz), SYSAPB PERI_CRG32[10] (24/50 MHz); completion is reported in PERI_CRG120. UARTs: PERI_CRG111[18..22] uart0..4_cksel (0 = 24 MHz, 1 = 6 MHz), gates PERI_CRG110[0..4], resets PERI_CRG110[5..9]. FMC (SPI NOR/NAND): PERI_CRG81[4:2] fmc_cksel (24/100/150/163/200/257/300/396 MHz; 300 and 396 MHz DDR mode only; the chip clock is the selected clock / 2 in SDR mode, / 4 in DDR mode), gate bit 1, reset bit 0. eMMC PERI_CRG82[3:2] (01 = 100, 10 = 50, 11 = 25 MHz), SDIO1 PERI_CRG85[3:2], SDIO0 PERI_CRG88[3:2] (same encoding). Ethernet PERI_CRG91 (core clock bit 7: 100/54 MHz, PHY clock-out [5:4], RMII source bit 2, gate bit 1, MAC reset bit 0, PHY reset bit 3). USB 2.0 PERI_CRG80. PWM PERI_CRG111[9:8] (3/50/24/24 MHz). Timers: there is no CRG select; the SP804 timers count 3 MHz or the system APB clock according to SYS_CTRL SC_CTRL timeren0ov..timeren7ov (bits 16..23).

    Cross-checks: the vendor-derived Linux driver of the Hi3516DV300 (OpenIPC `clk-hi3516dv300.c`, CRG at 0x12010000, same register layout) uses sysaxi 0x80[7:6] {24m, 200m, 300m}, sysapb 0x80[10] {24m, 50m}, fmc 0x144[4:2] {24, 100, 150, 163, 200, 257, 300, 396}, mmc 0x148 (eMMC), 0x154 (SDIO1) and 0x160 (SDIO0) [3:2] {100m, 50m, 25m} with values 1..3, uart 0x1BC[18..22] {24m, 6m}, pwm 0x1BC[9:8], eth 0x16C[7] {100m, 54m}, gates 0x1B8 (UART bits 0..4, I2C bits 11..18), 0x1BC (SPI 12..14, PWM 7, ADC), 0x194 (DMAC bits 1, 2), all identical to this data sheet. No vendor U-Boot for the Hi3516AV300 is in the tree (the arch-hi3516a/av200/hi3519 headers are other chips), so nothing from U-Boot was used.

    Known data sheet inconsistencies recorded in the register descriptions: Table 3-2 lists SYSAXI 198 MHz but PERI_CRG32 says 200 MHz; IVE default 475 MHz in Table 3-2 but PERI_CRG40 ive_cksel resets to 2 (300 MHz); PERI_CRG40, PERI_CRG61 and PERI_CRG63 have reserved rows with a non-zero reset value (modelled as reserved_nz fields); PERI_CRG_PLL122[10:0] in the text vs [3:0] in the table; PERI_CRG120 omits the EPLL POSTDIV DDR setting and Table 3-2 does not list it for DDR at all; PERI_CRG41 bit 2 is named sed_cksel but is a clock gate; PERI_CRG86 bit 19 name truncated; PERI_CRG111 rtc_srst_req described as `t_cap`; the register overview table is numbered `Table 3-1` although that number is already used in 3.1.2. The text layout dump has watermark noise in field names (`Cosensor1_cken`, `budmac_ckenCo`, ...) that was repaired from the PDF text.";

    reg {
        name = "APLL configuration register 0";
        desc = "APLL configuration register 0.

APLL (Cortex-A7/system PLL). In data sheet Fig. 3-3 only the grey EPLL and VPLL are marked user-programmable; the APLL and DPLL have fixed configurations. FOUTVCO = 24 MHz x (fbdiv + frac/2^24) / refdiv; FOUTPOSTDIV = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2). Reset: postdiv2 = 1, postdiv1 = 2, frac = 0; together with PERI_CRG_PLL1 (refdiv 1, fbdiv 75, integer mode) the APLL VCO runs at 1800 MHz and POSTDIV at 900 MHz (Fig. 3-3). Per Fig. 3-3 the APLL VCO output feeds the 600/360/300/257/200/100/72 MHz clocks and the POSTDIV output the 900 MHz and 450/150/50 MHz clocks.

Data sheet 3.2.6 PERI_CRG_PLL0 (offset 0x0, printed page 3-11, `hi3516av300--Hi3516AV300-Datasheet.txt` line 6614).";

        field {
            name = "apll_postdiv2";
            desc = "APLL second-stage output divider (postdiv2).";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_postdiv2[30:28];

        field {
            name = "apll_postdiv1";
            desc = "APLL first-stage output divider (postdiv1).";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x2;
        } apll_postdiv1[26:24];

        field {
            name = "apll_frac";
            desc = "APLL fractional part of the feedback multiplier (frac, 24 bits).";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_frac[23:0];
    } PERI_CRG_PLL0 @ 0x0;

    reg {
        name = "APLL configuration register 1";
        desc = "APLL configuration register 1.

APLL configuration register 1: power-down/bypass controls, refdiv and the integer multiplier. Reset 0x0100104B = dsmpd 1 (integer mode, apll_frac ignored), refdiv 1, fbdiv 0x4B = 75 -> VCO 24 x 75 = 1800 MHz. FOUTPOSTDIV = VCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2) = 900 MHz. Table 3-4 also lists FOUT1PH0, FOUT2, FOUT3, FOUT4 = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2 x 2/4/6/8). The valid VCO range is 800 MHz to 3.2 GHz (data sheet Table 3-4) and postdiv1 >= postdiv2.

Data sheet 3.2.6 PERI_CRG_PLL1 (offset 0x4, printed page 3-11, `hi3516av300--Hi3516AV300-Datasheet.txt` line 6644).";

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_bypass_enum {
            NOT_BYPASSED = 0 { name = "Not Bypassed"; desc = "Not bypassed"; };
            BYPASSED = 1 { name = "Bypassed"; desc = "Bypassed"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_bypass";
            desc = "APLL clock divider bypass control. 0: not bypassed, 1: bypassed.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_bypass_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_bypass[26:26];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_dacpd_enum {
            NORMAL = 0 { name = "Normal"; desc = "Normal operation"; };
            POWER_DOWN = 1 { name = "Power Down"; desc = "Power down"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_dacpd";
            desc = "APLL test signal control. 0: normal operation, 1: power down.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_dacpd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_dacpd[25:25];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_dsmpd_enum {
            FRACTIONAL = 0 { name = "Fractional"; desc = "Fractional mode"; };
            INTEGER = 1 { name = "Integer"; desc = "Integer mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_dsmpd";
            desc = "APLL fractional divider control. 0: fractional mode, 1: integer mode.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_dsmpd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_dsmpd[24:24];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_pd_enum {
            NORMAL = 0 { name = "Normal"; desc = "Normal operation"; };
            POWER_DOWN = 1 { name = "Power Down"; desc = "Power down"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_pd";
            desc = "APLL power-down control. 0: normal operation, 1: power down.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_pd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_pd[23:23];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_postdivpd_enum {
            CLOCK_OUTPUT = 0 { name = "Clock Output"; desc = "Normal clock output"; };
            NO_CLOCK_OUTPUT = 1 { name = "No Clock Output"; desc = "No clock output (the VCO clock is powered down as well)"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_postdivpd";
            desc = "APLL POSTDIV output power-down control. 0: normal clock output, 1: no clock output (the VCO clock is powered down as well).";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_postdivpd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_postdivpd[21:21];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_fout4phasepd_enum {
            CLOCK_OUTPUT = 0 { name = "Clock Output"; desc = "Normal clock output"; };
            NO_CLOCK_OUTPUT = 1 { name = "No Clock Output"; desc = "No clock output"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_fout4phasepd";
            desc = "APLL FOUT output power-down control. 0: normal clock output, 1: no clock output.";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_fout4phasepd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_fout4phasepd[20:20];

        field {
            name = "apll_refdiv";
            desc = "APLL reference clock divider (refdiv).";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_refdiv[17:12];

        field {
            name = "apll_fbdiv";
            desc = "APLL integer part of the feedback multiplier (fbdiv).";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x4B;
        } apll_fbdiv[11:0];
    } PERI_CRG_PLL1 @ 0x4;

    reg {
        name = "DPLL configuration register 0";
        desc = "DPLL configuration register 0.

DPLL, fixed configuration. Reset: postdiv2 = 1, postdiv1 = 4, frac = 0.

Data sheet 3.2.6 PERI_CRG_PLL2 (offset 0x8, printed page 3-12, `hi3516av300--Hi3516AV300-Datasheet.txt` line 6708).";

        field {
            name = "dpll_postdiv2";
            desc = "DPLL second-stage output divider (postdiv2).";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } dpll_postdiv2[30:28];

        field {
