All the selects reset to 0 = 24 MHz crystal, so the chip boots from the crystal and the boot code switches to the PLL clocks. After writing a select, poll the matching *_sc_seled field of PERI_CRG120. The selectable frequencies match data sheet Table 3-2 (A7: 24/600/792/900; DDR: 24/360/396/450 plus EPLL POSTDIV; SYSAXI: 24/200(198)/300; SYSCFG: 24/148.5; SYSAPB: 24/50 MHz). The vendor Linux driver (clk-hi3516dv300.c, same CRG layout) uses sysaxi 0x80[7:6] {24m, 200m, 300m} and sysapb 0x80[10] {24m, 50m}.

