    reg {
        name = "ADC/UART/SPI/OTP/IR/PWM clock and soft reset control register";
        desc = "ADC/UART/SPI/OTP/IR/PWM clock and soft reset control register.

ADC/UART/SPI/OTP/IR/PWM clock gates, selects and resets. Reset 0x01807883. Each of the five UARTs has its own clock select (uart0_cksel..uart4_cksel, bits 18..22): 0 = 24 MHz, 1 = 6 MHz; the vendor Linux driver uses uart mux at 0x1BC[18..22] {24m, 6m}, SPI gates at bits 12..14, PWM mux 0x1BC[9:8] {3m, 50m, 24m, 24m} and gate bit 7. The description of rtc_srst_req (bit 3) reads `t_cap soft reset request` (data sheet text).

Data sheet 3.2.6 PERI_CRG111 (offset 0x1BC, printed page 3-54, `hi3516av300--Hi3516AV300-Datasheet.txt` line 9605).";

